title: The cpanfile does not require LWP::Protocol::https; the API is HTTPS-only
updated: 2026-10-20T09:35:07Z
---

Both API base URLs are https: the Cloud API defaults to https://api.hetzner.cloud/v1 and the Robot API to https://robot-ws.your-server.de. The transport is LWP::UserAgent (WWW::Hetzner::LWPIO), and LWP::UserAgent only speaks https when LWP::Protocol::https is installed - otherwise it answers 501 with "Protocol scheme 'https' is not supported". The cpanfile declares LWP::UserAgent but not LWP::Protocol::https, so a fresh installation cannot reach the API at all.

Fix: declare LWP::Protocol::https as a runtime prerequisite next to LWP::UserAgent, and cover the declared HTTPS transport prerequisites with a test that reads the cpanfile (the pattern of p5-www-vastai and p5-www-picnic). A Changes entry notes the new prerequisite.

Note: the cpanfile audit of card #26 checked that every used module is declared; LWP::Protocol::https is not 'use'd anywhere, so the gap stayed invisible to it.

